{
  "$comment": "AUTHORITY for the surface of a Semiont client: every namespace, every method, the shape of what it returns, and what calling it does first. Every SDK is held to this table two ways. Its signatures are read by scripts/lint/check-client-surface.mjs, which fails on a method the table lacks, one an SDK lacks, and one whose return shape is not the row's. Its behaviour is run: each SDK's surface test calls every method as each of its `cases` states and holds what the call did to the row. A method name is the table's, in camelCase; an SDK spells it by its language's convention (`resourceContent` is `resource_content` in Rust), and a namespace whose name is a keyword there takes a trailing underscore (`yield_`, `match_`). An `events` row is a property named `<method>$` in TypeScript. `absent` names an SDK that does not have the method, and why: the lint then fails if that SDK has it, so an exemption that stopped being true is caught. Add a row here before adding a method to any SDK.",
  "shapes": {
    "promise": "Asked once, answered once: the value, or a failure with a code.",
    "stream": "A long-running operation: what it reports as it goes, then its final value. Awaited, it gives the final value.",
    "delegation": "A job another party does: the job's events as it goes, its completion the last of them. Awaited, it gives the completion.",
    "upload": "An upload in flight: its progress, then the id of the resource created.",
    "cache": "A live query. Building it touches nothing; its one-shot read asks the service now.",
    "signal": "Fire-and-forget. Nothing is returned and nothing is awaited.",
    "count": "A drive at the other participants: resolves with how many the gateway reached, or with no count when it kept none.",
    "events": "The events of one channel of the client's own bus, from now on.",
    "claims": "A worker's claims: each job it comes to hold, one at a time, from the first claim on. A held job starts, reports and settles itself."
  },
  "via": {
    "request": "A request of a bus operation, answered on its result or failure channel.",
    "emit": "A frame sent over the wire, with no reply awaited.",
    "local": "A frame published on the client's own bus and nowhere else.",
    "content": "An operation of the content transport: putBinary, getBinary, getBinaryStream or getResourceGraph.",
    "gateway": "One of the gateway's own operations: getCurrentUser, getMediaToken, getProtectedResourceMetadata, healthCheck or getStatus.",
    "observes": "The channel of the client's own bus whose frames an `events` row gives."
  },
